Options:
  --profile <name>    Set automation profile (win11_kvm, ubuntu_r620_kvm, real_hardware)
  --no-proxy          Bypass corporate proxy (direct internet access)
  --proxy-url <url>   Use custom proxy URL instead of corporate default
  --proxy             Force corporate proxy (default behavior)

Actions:
  deploy    [targets] — Build VMs (idempotent, skips existing)
  redeploy  [targets] — Force-delete + fresh deploy
  destroy   [targets] — Tear down VMs (full teardown if no targets)
  validate  [targets] — Re-run SSH connectivity checks
  test      <type>    — Deploy single VM for testing (sonic|ubuntu|chr)
  ssh       <vm>      — SSH directly into a VM
  console   <vm>      — Attach virsh console to a VM
  status              — Show all VM states + resource usage
  images              — Download and verify images only
  tools               — Download/install platform tools (Helm, kubectl, Kubespray, etc.)

Targets (optional, default=all):
  Single:   Spine_S1, Leaf_L2, Host12_1, Exit_Router1
  Multiple: Spine_S1,Leaf_L1,Host12_1  (comma-separated)
  Groups:   spines, leafs, border_leafs, switches, servers, routers, all

Proxy examples:
  deploy_lab_v13.sh --no-proxy --profile win11_kvm deploy          # Direct internet (home lab)
  deploy_lab_v13.sh --proxy-url http://myproxy:3128 deploy         # Custom proxy
  deploy_lab_v13.sh --profile win11_kvm deploy                     # Corporate proxy (default)

Examples:
  deploy_lab_v13.sh --profile win11_kvm deploy                     # Deploy all 17 VMs
  deploy_lab_v13.sh --profile ubuntu_r620_kvm redeploy spines      # Redeploy only spines
  deploy_lab_v13.sh --no-proxy --profile win11_kvm tools           # Download platform tools (no proxy)
  deploy_lab_v13.sh --profile win11_kvm validate Leaf_L1,Leaf_L2   # Validate specific leafs
  deploy_lab_v13.sh --profile win11_kvm test sonic                 # Deploy single SONiC for testing
  deploy_lab_v13.sh --profile win11_kvm ssh Spine_S1               # SSH into Spine_S1
